    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p11-q15-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Given the rectangles have dimensions $6\\text{ cm}\\times30\\text{ cm}$, find the perimeter and area of the cross.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$P=120\\text{ cm}$ and $A=324\\text{ cm}^2$.",
          "worked": "The overlap is a $6\\text{ cm}\\times6\\text{ cm}$ square. Each of the eight longer boundary segments has length $\\frac{(30-6)}{2}=12\\text{ cm}.$\n$$\\begin{align*}P&=8\\times12+4\\times6\\\\P&=120\\text{ cm}\\\\A&=2(30\\times6)-6^2\\\\A&=324\\text{ cm}^2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p11-q15-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Given the area of the cross is $28\\text{ cm}^2$ and its perimeter is $32\\text{ cm}$, find the dimensions of the rectangles.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p11-q15-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "2\\text{ cm}\\times8\\text{ cm}",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p11-q15-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The perimeter gives the length; subtract the square overlap when finding the area.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Let the rectangle length be $L$ cm and its width be $w$ cm, with $0<w<L$. The exterior has eight segments of length $\\frac{(L-w)}{2}$ and four of length $w$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P&=8\\left(\\frac{L-w}{2}\\right)+4w\\\\P&=4L\\\\L&=\\frac{32}{4}\\\\L&=8\\end{align*}$$\nSubtract the square overlap:\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=2Lw-w^2\\\\28&=16w-w^2\\\\28&=w(16-w)\\end{align*}$$\nThe width is an integer between 1 and 7. Checking these values, only $w=2$ gives $w(16-w)=2\\times14=28$. The rectangles are $2\\text{ cm}\\times8\\text{ cm}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 102
      }
    ]
  },
